content.text:
Use the `@variant` directive in your CSS with the breakpoint name, for example `@variant md { … }`.

```css
:root {
  --my-var: 1rem;

  @variant md {
    --my-var: 2rem;
  }
}
```

- `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, "Using custom CSS → Using variants" (lines 299–400) documents `@variant` for applying Tailwind variants in custom CSS. Its examples use `dark`, `hover` and `focus`, not a breakpoint. Applying it to `md` is my inference, because breakpoints are variants too. The `:root` example above is also mine.
- `src/docs/theme.mdx`, "Relationship to variants" (lines 103–127) says `--breakpoint-*` theme variables define the responsive variants. That is why `md` and the other names work as variants.
- To add your own breakpoint names, see `src/docs/responsive-design.mdx`, "Using custom breakpoints" (lines 299–331).

